/P 155 0 R
/E (Before we teach a single trick, before we shape a single behavior, we need to understand who we are working with.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (A dog is not a small human. A dog is not a robot. A dog is a living, breathing, feeling being with instincts, emotions, and a view of the world that is completely different from ours.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (Dogs experience the world nose-first. Their sense of smell is tens of thousands of times stronger than ours. They read body language faster than we can speak. They feel tension in a leash, joy in a voice, and uncertainty in hesitation.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (When we understand this, everything changes.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
