/P 177 0 R
/E (The golden rule of the 3 D's is this: if one goes up, another should come down.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
471 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E (If you are increasing duration, reduce distractions. If you are adding distance, shorten the duration. If the environment is full of distractions, stay close and keep it brief.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
472 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E (This is not about lowering your expectations. It is about being strategic. You are building your dog's confidence and capability one layer at a time.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
